.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_confidence_matrix" "fuzzygene_confidence_matrix"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_confidence_matrix \- Export the confidence matrix of a trained model (same shape as the weight matrix).
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_confidence_matrix(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
\fBlayout\fR as string = "square", 
\fBminConfidence\fR as double = 0, 
\fBgenes\fR as string = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Export the confidence matrix of a trained model (same shape as the weight matrix).
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBlayout\fB \fR\- \fBsquare\fR (default), \fBregulators\fR or \fBcompact\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBminConfidence\fB \fR\- edges with a smaller confidence are exported as zero; 0 keeps all. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgenes\fB \fR\- restrict the exported rows to these target genes; empty means all. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a Matrix object (rows = targets, columns = regulators, non negative values)
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Rows and columns are exactly the same as in \fBfuzzygene_regulation_matrix\fR (same layout,
 same order), only the element value changes: `W[i, j]` becomes the confidence of the
 edge `j -> i`, that is the prior confidence when the edge is supported by the prior
 network and the absolute expression correlation `|Pearson|` otherwise.
 


 


 Weight and confidence answer two different questions ("how strong / which direction" vs
 "how trustworthy"), so exporting both matrices and using weight for the edge width and
 confidence for the edge opacity or a cutoff is the usual combination:
 
\fB
 let w = fuzzygene::fuzzygene_regulation_matrix(model, layout = "compact");
 let c = fuzzygene::fuzzygene_confidence_matrix(model, layout = "compact");
 geneExpression::write.expr_matrix(w, file = "/path/weight.csv", id = "geneID");
 geneExpression::write.expr_matrix(c, file = "/path/confidence.csv", id = "geneID");
 
\fR`
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
